{
 "info": {
 "title": "Ozone Connect - UAE Insurance API Description",
 "description": "## Ozone Connect - UAE Insurance API Description\n\nThis document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html) for Insurance APIs for Ozone Connect.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by a financial institution to facilitate integration with the API Hub.\n\n### Versioning\n\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where: \n\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n\n### v2.2.2\n\n* Changed every date-time field to reference the shared `AEDateTime` Schema Object. `AEDateTime` states that a\n date-time value identifies an instant, that the offset is part of the value and must be applied by the\n recipient, and that two encodings of the same instant are equivalent and must behave identically. It carries\n a `pattern` requiring an offset and forbidding `-00:00`; all other offsets remain conformant. Each field\n description now states only what is specific to that field. Per OFP-014.\n\n\n### v2.2.1\n\n\n* Added the optional `PolicyEndDate` property to the `get /life-insurance-policies` response, which was the only\n insurance policy list schema not to carry it. It matches the `PolicyEndDate` in the corresponding UAE Insurance\n API description response, which is an unconstrained string described as the date on which cover ends, rather than\n the `format: date` property used by the other insurance types.\n\n\n* Changed the `get /{industryType}-insurance-policies/{InsurancePolicyId}` operation to return\n `CreditDebitIndicator` within `Premium.Adjustments`, indicating whether a premium adjustment is a credit,\n reducing the premium payable, or a debit, increasing the premium payable. `CreditDebitIndicator` and\n `AdjustmentAmount` are both mandatory for each entry in `Adjustments`.\n\n\n* Removed the `maximum` of 100 from `AEInsuranceServiceRatingRateOrRatio`, which is referenced by the\n `ServiceRating` properties `SolvencyRatio`, `ClaimsPaymentCapacityRatio`, `AverageClaimSettlementTime`, and\n `CustomerComplaintRate`. None of these is a 0-100 percentage: both ratios routinely exceed 100% for a solvent\n insurer, and the other two are measured in calendar days and in complaints per 1,000 active policies\n respectively. The two genuine percentages, `ClaimSettlementRatio` and `ClaimRejectionRate`, now reference a new\n `AEInsuranceServiceRatingPercentage` schema, which retains `maximum: 100` and adds `minimum: 0`.\n\n\n### v2.1.3\n\n\n* Changed the `get /{insurance-type}-insurance-quotes/{QuoteId}` operation to return the correct type for `Pending`\n `QuoteStatus` responses.\n\n\n### v2.1.2\n\n\n* Changed the `insurancePolicyIds` parameter from optional to mandatory for the `get /{industryType}-insurance-policies` operation.\n\n\n* Changed the guidance for `insurancePolicyIds` parameter for the `get /{industryType}-insurance-policies` operation.\n\n\n### v2.1.1\n\n\n* Initial version that delivers v2.1 requirements (see separate, detailed changelog for changes from last v2.1.x version).\n\n",
 "version": "v2.2.2"
 },
